  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_SPECS` | `specs/README.md` absent, or no approved scope spec to scaffold |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Tasks exist + mode verb absent (per `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`) |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule reference does not resolve to an existing file (`AX_RULES_RESOLUTION_HARD_FAIL`) |
    | `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` | An in-scope spec lacks a Bootstrap Requirements section (did not pass the scope flow) |
    | `H_ID_COLLISION` | A generated Task-ID / slug collides with an existing one |
    | `H_TYPING_SCENARIO_MISSING` | A DbC contract in Spec References has no `contract`-level typing scenario mapped to a test |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the breakdown or the test plan |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Read the Portal; detect scopes, graph, mode. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read `specs/README.md` Scope Graph (absent → `H_NO_SPECS`); read each ✅ scope spec and its
        module specs. Detect the graph (`AX_SCOPE_GRAPH_DETECTION`) and mode
        (`AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`); `extend-dag` reads existing tickets and preserves their IDs
        (`AX_EXTEND_DAG_PRESERVES_EXISTING_IDS`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CASCADE">
      <Goal>Resolve the rules cascade. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the rule registry. Per scope, take the transitive closure of depends-on edges and collect
        rule refs (`AX_RULES_CASCADE_RESOLUTION`); every ref must resolve to a file
        (`AX_RULES_RESOLUTION_HARD_FAIL`, else `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`). Build per-scope Cascade Tables. No
        operator stop — mechanical.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_DAG">
      <Goal>Build the acyclic task DAG. — GATE 1: operator approves the BREAKDOWN.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Bootstrap Requirements per spec → Phase-0 bootstrap tickets (`AX_BOOTSTRAP_TICKET_DERIVATION`);
        missing section → `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING`. Form tickets per
        `AX_DAG_AND_TICKET_BOUNDARIES` (one per coherent spec unit; subdivide only for parallelism or
        context overflow); cross-scope placement per `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_TASK_PLACEMENT`; assign slugs
        (`AX_TASK_ID_UNIQUENESS`). Acyclic. **Present the DAG (the breakdown) as a decision card and
        get operator approval — this is the one gate on structure.** STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_TASK_GENERATION">
      <Goal>Generate tickets + test plan. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/task-ticket-structure.xml")`. Per ticket:
        decompose into phases (`AX_PHASES_DECLARED_IN_HEADER`; impl and test always separate); per-phase
        `Rules:` links via `AX_RULE_ACTIVATION_PLAN`; draft BDD with the mandatory `contract`-level
        typing scenario per contract (`AX_TICKET_HAS_BDD_AND_TESTS`); pre-fill the Execution Log plan
        (`AX_EXECUTION_LOG_PLAN_VS_FACT`). **BDD coverage pass — dispatch ONE isolated subagent** with a
        clean slice (module spec + contract anchors + requirements + draft BDD) asking «which negative /
        corner / trust-boundary / failure-mode scenarios are missing?»; merge approved ones, log the
        reviewed checklist in the ticket Decision Log. Validate every contract has its typing scenario
        mapped to a test (else `H_TYPING_SCENARIO_MISSING`). No operator stop — automated.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_TEST_PLAN_REVIEW">
      <Goal>GATE 2: operator approves the TEST PLAN.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present the test plan as a decision card: each BDD scenario as a use-case, tagged
        `[<ACRONYM>-REQ-N]`, traced up to the scope Vision / goal it protects, plus coverage (every
        contract has a typing scenario, every scenario maps to a test). The operator approves **what is
        tested, which use-cases are covered, and that this guarantees the vision** — the one gate on
        substance. Out-of-scope proposals the subagent surfaced are raised here. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Write the index hierarchy; hand off. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-tasks-index.xml")` and write each
        `<module>.3-tasks.md` (Tracker, Slug Registry, intra-module DAG, shared content per
        `AX_TICKET_DEDUPLICATION`). Roll up the scope tracker
        (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/scope-tasks-index.xml")`) and
        the project index (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/project-tasks-index.xml")`).
        Then run `sdd-check --all .` (task-DAG: id-collisions · deps resolve · acyclic; tracker↔ticket sync;
        phase graph; exec-log) and resolve or consciously defer every finding per
        `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK` — the scaffold mutation is done only once the task graph passes.
        Emit a created-files summary with traceability links. Hand off to execute (isolated, cheaper
        model). No operator stop.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    Service line — dim, internal, kept silent (per `AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`):
    `📋 TS_R<N> · <scope> · <mode> · conf=<LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH>`. Breadcrumb milestones (per
    `BREADCRUMB_FORMAT`): Intake · Cascade · DAG · Tickets · Tests · Done. Only two milestones are
    operator gates — DAG (breakdown) and Tests (test plan).

